      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Not a bug, the behavior is documented: https://creators.vrchat.com/avatars/#proxy-animations\n\nThis may be a feature request. There are legitimate use cases to have built-in proxy animations in animators too, and something like `proxy_foobar` will not be replaced if a built-in animation with that name doesn't exist.\n\nAre you proposing the SDK to display a warning when a built-in proxy animation name (based on a static list) with a mismatching GUID is used?",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-10-26T15:32:11.667Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "If you don't rename the hand gesture animations after copying them from the VRChat SDK, VRChat will keep using the default ones\n\nThere should be a warning about that in the SDK when you use an animation with a name that starts with proxy_!",
